## My role in building this

This project is also a bit different from some of my previous work.

For earlier projects in the Playground, I spent much more time writing the implementation myself.

For this one, I deliberately tried something different.

I already had the creative direction and the problem I wanted to explore.

I knew what I wanted the simulation to represent;

how I wanted the elevators to move, what the passengers should do, what the architecture should look like,

and what I eventually wanted to experiment with.

So instead of spending most of my time manually implementing every part, I used AI heavily to help turn the design into code.

That changed the speed of the project a lot.

I could spend more of my time thinking about:

* the simulation design
* the physics
* the state transitions
* what should be separated into different modules
* what the system should eventually allow
